{
  "id": "bracket-order",
  "title": "Bracket Order",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [
    "recursion",
    "arrays"
  ],
  "description": "A single-elimination bracket for `n` players (where `n` is a power of two, at least 2) is seeded so that, if the higher seed always wins, seed 1 and seed 2 can only meet in the final, seeds 1 to 4 can only meet in the semifinals, and so on.\n\nThe bracket for 2 players is `[1, 2]`. To build the bracket for `2m` players from the bracket for `m` players, replace every seed `s` with the pair `s, 2m + 1 - s`.\n\nReturn the bracket, read top to bottom, as a list of seeds. Adjacent entries (positions 0 and 1, 2 and 3, ...) play each other in round one.",
  "function": {
    "name": "bracketOrder",
    "pythonName": "bracket_order",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "n",
        "type": "integer"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "integer[]"
  },
  "compare": {
    "mode": "exact"
  },
